     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><br><div><div>On Apr 12, 2013, at 6:04 AM, Pierpa wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">...just for the record. It seems my problem was simply that the GTK+ ver that rattle() automatically downloads (v2.18.5) is not the correct one.<div>I just downloaded and installed v2.24.17 from <a href=\"http://r.research.att.com/#other\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r.research.att.com/%23other&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478937367000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3JpPqmcT7MBEyqMRMx-AQv\">http://r.research.att.com/#other</a> and everything seems to work now...make sense?</div></blockquote><div><br></div>It does make sense. The v2.24 version is labeled as suitable for R 3.0.0. You seem to be the first one to have gotten success, though. Maybe you could post your successful setup in more detail so those of us who are still getting segfaults can learn from you? Is GTK+ installed as a framework. What is your PATH?</div><div><br></div><div>--  </div><br><div>\r\n<span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><span style